  "description": "EQURAN crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H90 Gd6 N40 O22. From the CIF bond table, Gd01 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd02 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd03 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.769-4.263 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.39-125.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd6(OH)6(NO3)4(bmptm)4(DMF)4]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
